 "notes": "Libretto by Emanuel Schikaneder (1791). Words as printed in the Edition Peters vocal score, which the app follows where it differs from the libretto: \"Zu Hülfe!\" (the libretto has \"Hilfe\"), \"Ungeheu'r\", \"Heldenthat\" and \"ertheilen\" in the old spelling, \"geseh'n\", \"vor'ge\", \"Ruh'\" and \"bleib'\" with the print's apostrophes, and the many repeats of the music (\"ich bleibe\", \"ich wache\", \"ich schütze\" and the closing \"ich!\" are the music's). Tamino sings until he faints (bar 40); then each Lady has her own line. IPA follows sung German stage diction: final -er, -ern as [ɐ]; the prefixes er-, ver-, zer- with [ɛr]; r elsewhere rolled or flipped; ch as [ç] after front vowels and [x] after back vowels; glottal stops [ʔ] before initial vowels; final b d g devoiced.",
